  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The standard MongoDB connection string has the form `mongodb://[username:password@]host1[:port1][,...hostN[:portN]][/[defaultauthdb][?options]]`: credentials are optional, the host list can contain multiple `host[:port]` entries, and the database path and query options are optional. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/connection-string-formats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2828c2eefcc790cb137f5d289972aec0b7afec31819f6b1cf340069b33b78153",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9660b47027675942ee35c8b7697c1d8ced4c51bef55edf51b2c60875f91d2c00",
            "ev:b525820df186f2a156dd39fc844c2f8f32a862c46302b9e7986a07664bea41bb"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "When a port is omitted from a standard MongoDB URI, the default port is `27017`. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/connection-string-formats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:aee22d09418193e4d6d0218c8bce6acfbfc8dc4e2fe27bc2e8c6aa68debfd9f5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4fc50b5f817f262612af2fa03d06c71d410970b82e3d5e1abcbe06874fad8c67",
            "ev:824d7a9ba7a1a0fa150ec2b0bd6211ee8301953f0b76fa4da2c4247b286b9899"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The MongoDB driver specification describes connection strings as URI-style but says their grammar does not conform to RFC 3986 and cannot be parsed by generic URI parsers; applications need a parser that understands MongoDB connection strings. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/connection-string/connection-string-spec.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e6f0c0fa77e79e8864df92e2d126130b262852ebe1ec4e3b4f86f54cf023baf9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:8d2ee4902f509645836d91bc531f566794a63667acf3d1c194a5ee0973e4ca64",
            "ev:beb4ba9627ffd794ba8e60b6fe47648ab8ff20705719f92119d4f0084ff99163",
            "ev:f988fba1c5860f2c3c053b6a670f1e24a33cc86ece59dd8f0a94824839e703d2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The SRV form is `mongodb+srv://[username:password@]host[/[defaultauthdb][?options]]`; it accepts one hostname without an explicit port, then the driver queries DNS SRV records to discover the hosts. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/connection-string-formats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3afcc53f4abf52fdd935af21cff767bb2f39ffa0495c2d74c03168dda99edc13",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:abb09bf7e0c23e40d13e41577afb0c0f6fd72450152a14df18362eb1a169f61c",
            "ev:ad8c275af93d9fddf2e339b33cb38bb6ad4b84d9f6b69f74f48f18dc36e81afe",
            "ev:dbfcce6466be3145823319985724473361a615b60774b09a678428198b8ed215"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Connection options use `?name=value` query parameters; if options appear without a database path, include `/` between the last host and `?`. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/connection-string-formats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:966bc41c7ee37913a8fd4a0b73841748c92a7ba545796845080ba4b0138ae6a7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b5bd6e548dacd9c7d8357cfb12cd8873b1f6fcc217f17abed8ea1c399e76b8e1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For portable credentials, percent-encode `$ : / ? # [ ] @` in MongoDB usernames and passwords. RFC 3986 defines a percent-encoded octet as `%` followed by two hexadecimal digits; the MongoDB connection-string specification says drivers should follow RFC 3986 userinfo rules but may accept some reserved characters unencoded for backward compatibility. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/connection-string-formats.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:021f96ba4cac6ed95d27bf608ba7bb542db3bdd578285eba0af360262303322f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:85ab4299ca23bf7963c9799d1ac2ca1842939558d4a1bf79c18431067e88f752",
            "ev:9d72696aae1cdd5e44307122c42f4d8ac78c8c1a8115ec97b4fa10b2db80c924",
            "ev:e77a46a52647314e9693e7605f50773700e555325c3ea15266488c4573620961"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MongoDB's current documentation differs on replica-set seed completeness: the Manual says standard connection strings require all cluster members, while the SDAM specification and current .NET/C# guide describe discovery from a seed list containing one or more members. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/connection-string/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:535fb514d1a9ab5d9dbd85de24e262e09b1e3860a458300f046b7d2fb5c35521",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
